## 🧪 Model Overfitting Analysis

> [!CAUTION]
> **Verdict: The model is almost certainly overfitting**, but not for the reason you might think.

### Evidence

1. **Validation data leakage** — The validation set is a subset of the training set. This means:
   - Training accuracy ≈ Validation accuracy (because they share data)
   - Test accuracy (on truly unseen data) would be significantly lower
   - The "good" validation metrics are an illusion

2. **No regularization** — No Dropout, no L2 regularization, no data augmentation at training time. With a frozen base model and only a Dense(13) head, the model has **~16,653 trainable parameters** (1280 × 13 + 13). This is relatively few, but with a small dataset and data leakage, overfitting is still likely.

3. **Static augmentation only** — Pre-generated augmentations are static. The model sees the same augmented images every epoch, essentially memorizing them. Runtime augmentation ensures each epoch sees slightly different transforms, acting as regularization.

4. **Wrong normalization** — The model receives inputs in [0, 1] but MobileNetV2's pretrained weights expect [-1, 1]. The pretrained features are partially unusable, forcing the small head layer to compensate, which increases overfitting risk.

### Why This Matters

Your current model appears to work in demo scenarios but will likely fail on:
- Images taken with different cameras/lighting
- Images at different angles or backgrounds
- Images with multiple leaves or partial occlusion
- Leaves in different seasons (color variation)

